WEBVTT

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:23.870
It's coming.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.590
Ouch...

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:32.760
What's going on?

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.140
<b>Quest 03     Roleplay</b>

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.140
I thought I was going to die.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.980
We cleared it,

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.640
but it's become routine for us 
to fight as a pair.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:28.240
What?

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.710
At this rate, we won't experience 
the true joy of <i>PSO2</i>.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.710
True joy?

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.940
Connecting with others through association.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.030
Oh...

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:49.520
"The true joy of <i>PSO2</i> is connecting 
with others through association."

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.980
Don't look!

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:55.210
The bonds between ARKS members
 makes them strong.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:57.530
I see. I'll add that.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:01.550
Sasaki-kun, why aren't the 
meeting documents ready yet?

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:05.030
Sorry. I had a career meeting
 with my teacher.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.790
I don't need your excuses. 
Just hurry up and do it.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.040
Okay. Sorry.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.180
What's going on?

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.600
Vice President.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.310
Go to the faculty office immediately.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.480
And get this stamped.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:17.050
Okay.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.550
After that, give this key 
to the basketball team.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.450
On the double.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:23.930
Got it.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.880
Tachibana-kun.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.000
Once you're finished with that, 
could you help Sasaki-kun?

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:29.930
O-Okay.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:33.440
S-Sorry for the inconvenience.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.940
What? It's fine.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.610
We finished all the jobs we were told to do.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:48.990
I'm really sorry.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.340
You don't need to keep apologizing.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.320
Apologies are meaningless if you 
don't use them at the right time.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.840
Right, Yu-chan?

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:59.340
What's Yu-chan?

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:02.290
What? Isn't your name Sasaki Yutaka?

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.340
That makes you Yu-chan.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.430
That's not what I meant.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.970
Are you the kind of guy who 
says that to his friends?

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.850
Since we're both tasked with grunt work,

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.770
I thought we could get to know each other.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.640
Grunt work?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.350
In any case, please don't say that.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.730
Huh? Maybe I came on too strong.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:22.860
Tachibana-kun.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.770
I already finished my report.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:27.080
I'll go print it out.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.000
I see.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.870
It seems you're even capable of doing 
student council work pretty well.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.550
It's all odd jobs, though.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:36.560
You just joined the student 
council the other day.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:38.250
Whether it's odd jobs or anything else,

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:41.740
it's important to connect with 
others through association.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:45.680
Connect with others through association?

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.100
Party play? Mr. Aloof?

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:51.240
He said, "Connecting with 
others through association

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.470
is the true joy of <i>PSO2</i>."

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.470
Even though he's SORO the Aloof Warrior?

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:57.480
I know, right?

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.860
He doesn't group with anyone himself.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.860
It is how most people play, though.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.360
Is that right?

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.740
Maybe it's just Mr. Aloof's 
next lesson for you.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.010
I guess.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.240
But he's the only one I know.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.500
Then why don't we play together today?

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.000
You mean...

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:17.830
The meet is over.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.750
I'm free.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:22.760
Where's Kota?

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:23.920
You there!

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:34.070
I regret that I've allowed 
so much time to pass,

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.470
but, my friend,

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:39.120
let us depart on our eternal adventure.

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:41.020
Hey, wait.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:41.570
What?

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:44.370
Is this you?

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:45.070
Yeah.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.820
What, what, what?
What's gotten into you?

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.220
What do you mean?

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:50.570
Your character is nothing like you.

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:52.170
What are you talking about?

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.330
I'm roleplaying.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.830
Roleplaying?

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:56.250
Yeah.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.780
In these kinds of games, 
you have to become your character.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:01.780
And this is my character's personality.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:02.840
What?

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:06.430
And why are you using your real name, anyway?

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:07.340
You'll get doxxed.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:08.590
Doxxed?

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:10.450
As in, your real life will be exposed.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:14.670
It means people will know your 
character is Tachibana Itsuki.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.100
Hey, the regulars.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:18.100
Regulars?

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.550
Koa, it's been a while.

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:23.480
We were worried you quit.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.410
We've been waiting for you.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:26.860
Long time, no see.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.910
Let's heat things up together today.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:29.570
Yeah.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.810
While my soul was absent,

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:35.700
it was occupying a body in another world

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.250
where I was engaged in combat 
with powerful opponents

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.110
and companions who speak with their fists.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.630
A karate tournament, huh?

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.780
You understood that?

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:45.090
How'd it go?

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:47.380
My chest was adorned with a white star.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.340
You won.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.090
And you won?

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.850
Hey, that's Itsuki-san.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.100
What? You know who I am?

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:57.790
He always groups with Mr. Aloof.

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:58.560
I see.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.100
Itsuki, are you Koa's friend?

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.410
Well, actually...

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.860
Itsuki and I are connected in the real world.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:07.610
You're IRL friends.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:09.850
Kota.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:10.670
Yeah?

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:12.150
What are IRL friends?

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:14.730
It means we're friends "in real life."

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.710
Not just online, but regular friends.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.170
Huh...

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:25.380
By the way, we've been 
plagued by a troll lately.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.630
Ah, the despicable and accursed 
creatures of darkness.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.340
I don't like him.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:33.990
He got Last Samurai and Yumiko, too.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:35.890
It was awful.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.360
I won't play with him again.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.230
You two should be careful.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:44.230
I shall.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:47.110
What do trolls do in-game?

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:52.110
They bother other players with 
their outrageous behavior.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.620
Is that fun?

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.230
I'm not sure.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:00.410
They must do it because they think it's fun.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:02.370
I guess all kinds of people play.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:05.250
Aren't these guys interesting, though?

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:08.380
They enjoy roleplaying by 
altering their speech patterns.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:11.380
Yeah. It's like playing pretend.

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.420
I've never met them in real life, though.

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:18.390
As long as we're here, why don't we 
try some multi-party play with them?

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:20.600
Sure!

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:26.310
<b>[Roleplay]
</b>The original meaning of the word is to undergo a simulated learning experience while playing a particular role. In online games, it means creating a backstory for the character you control and changing your appearance or the way you speak accordingly. It is also the origin of the term RPG (Roleplaying Game).

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:30.900
<b>[Party Play]
</b>The act of two or more players joining together to create a "party" and going on adventures or battling together in online games. In PSO2, parties can be as large as four people, but multiple parties may fight on the same field with up to 12 people in "multi-party play."

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:46.200
Yumiko!

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.420
Nezumi!

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.300
There's one over there, too!

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.930
Leave it to me!

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:08.940
All right.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:12.690
What?

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.360
Overconfidence is your greatest enemy.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:18.780
So cool.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.120
That was seriously fun.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.620
It changed how I fight, too.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:29.760
It felt like a completely different 
game from playing as a pair.

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:31.630
R-Really? That's great.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.480
By the way,

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:36.860
could you pick up the samples we requested 
from the construction company?

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:37.700
Sure.

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.600
Tachibana-kun, before that,

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:44.350
could you put these posters up on 
the bulletin boards around school?

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:45.820
Got it.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:47.600
I'm off to do some odd jobs.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.690
Just how many bulletin boards 
does this school have?

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:57.580
I haven't made a dent in these posters.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:01.350
I'll put these up.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:01.950
What?

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.950
Don't you have something else to do?

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.460
Yu-chan.

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:10.080
I told you not to call me that.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:13.110
Really? You'll really do it?

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:14.340
Y-Yeah...

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:15.960
Thanks, Yu-chan.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.220
Sorry for making you come out here.

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:23.190
I'll go get them. You can 
wait in the break room.

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:24.070
Okay.

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:26.100
Now, where did I put those?

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.020
Did you finish assembling the pipes?

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:28.740
Yeah.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:30.400
Then we can start installing them.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:31.450
Yeah.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:33.860
By the way, that guy Itsuki 
we grouped with yesterday...

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.520
He had some serious backbone.

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:37.710
Yeah.

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:40.160
I thought he only grouped with Mr. Aloof.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:40.990
<i>Who are they?</i>

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:44.860
You won't have any energy
 if all you eat is vegetables.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:45.870
Have some meat.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.560
But it's organic.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:49.460
What's that?

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:53.000
Hey, is your name OrgaCats 
because you eat organic food?

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:57.060
Yeah, didn't I tell you?

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:59.680
Actually, I find your name, 
Master Nezumi, more mysterious.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.080
I'm Master Nezumi because I'm the boss.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.180
Then you should translate 
"Nezumi" into English, too.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:09.200
What? Master... Mouse, huh?

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.190
Nezumi sounds better.

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:14.690
I guess you're right.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.070
All right!

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.690
Once we're finished with work,
 let's play some <i>PSO2</i>.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:19.950
Sure.

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:23.220
Boss, you need to learn to fight already.

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:24.260
Shut up.

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:28.200
Thanks for waiting.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.260
Here are the material samples.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.340
I was playing with those guys?

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:33.960
What?

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.460
I'm back.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:43.240
Everyone left?

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:47.600
Dear Itsuki-kun,
Good work today.
This was left over from the meeting,
but you're welcome to have it.
Your grunt work partner

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:50.260
Yu-chan...

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:52.850
What a nice guy.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.360
So Nezumi and Cats are 
physical laborers, huh?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.610
I was seriously surprised.

00:11:58.090 --> 00:12:02.110
A lot of people create characters the
 exact opposite of their real personalities.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:03.610
Really?

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:10.860
I want to play in a big group
 like we did yesterday.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:14.620
Then let us approach some of the 
people wandering around here.

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:15.560
Sure.

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:18.500
SORO-san.

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.030
Ah, Itsuki.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.470
Is this your friend?

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:26.790
My name is Koa.

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:28.970
Itsuki and I are connected in the real world.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.730
It's a pleasure to meet you, SORO-dono.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.780
It's nice to meet you.

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:37.730
It seems you're playing with others, as well.

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:40.230
Did you enjoy playing in a party?

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.370
Yeah.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:43.400
Thanks to Koa, I made more friends.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:46.740
And like you said, multi-party play is fun.

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:48.180
I see.

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:50.240
That's good.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.370
I know. SORO-san, why don't 
you group up with us?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:54.870
What?

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:57.560
You must get lonely always 
playing by yourself.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:58.690
Indeed.

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:02.670
Abandoning your aloof ways and
taking the main road is one way to go,

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:03.510
Mr. Forever Alone.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:04.980
Don't call me forever alone!

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.510
Besides, I'm not lonely.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:09.640
Now we've got three.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.740
Should we add someone else?

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:14.520
I wouldn't mind giving you a hand.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.770
We've got one empty spot. Why not?

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:22.780
Very well.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.220
Now, let's get going.

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:28.780
What is that?

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:32.680
The dragonkin are here already.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.490
Let's split up and deal with them.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:35.230
Got it.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:36.460
My friends!

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:41.320
I swear on my fists that 
we shall be victorious

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:43.820
in this battle!

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:47.020
Is he always like this?

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:48.230
Apparently.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.220
Hey! You're not going to fight with us?

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:55.320
What? Grunts belong with grunts.

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:58.360
You guys deal with them.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:01.070
Try not to bother me.

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.730
Is he not going to fight?

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.110
This is the guy the regulars mentioned.

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:07.360
He's the troll.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:14.370
Musashi!

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:16.370
Heal Itsuki.

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:18.400
Musashi!

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:22.380
What? Heal yourself, you pest.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.750
You've at least got Monomates, right?

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:27.050
Itsuki is a beginner.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.360
He needs your support.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:33.020
If he keeps relying on others, 
he'll be a beginner forever.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:36.270
Now deal with them already, you oaf.

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:39.060
So this is a troll.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:41.010
You...

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:42.070
What?

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:44.900
I can't believe you took so long
 to kill some grunts.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.680
You half-wits.

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:48.400
Hey, you didn't do anything!

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:49.570
What?

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:52.640
You've got no right to talk 
when you're struggling

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:54.910
to deal with those enemies.

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.960
Hey, wait!

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:01.320
Hey, it's him.

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:03.920
Looks like he did it again.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.290
What an idiot.

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:06.170
Yeah.

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:10.840
I'm pissed!

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:15.240
I should've listened more 
closely to the regulars.

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:15.850
Huh?

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:17.850
A friend request?

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:20.490
What? I don't believe it.

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:22.100
I'm blocking him.

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:23.360
No, wait!

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:24.540
What?

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:27.960
Through grouping up over the past few days,

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:31.790
I've realized there's a real flesh-and-blood 
person behind each character.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:34.240
That's what makes trolls unforgivable.

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.740
But the same goes for Musashi.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:40.120
We'll understand if we talk to him.

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:42.620
You're right.

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:45.560
I'm going to go talk to Musashi.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:49.630
Hey, Musashi.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.120
Wait up.

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:54.860
You're one of the pests from earlier.

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:56.140
What do you want?

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:59.140
Why do you troll other players?

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:02.020
What? Troll?

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:05.150
Is that what you came here to say?

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:09.530
Don't you know there are real people 
on the other side of the screen?

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:11.030
What?

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:13.910
You don't need to tell 
me that! That's obvious!

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:17.520
And I know who you are!

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:20.480
Want me to expose your identity? Huh?

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:21.910
I don't mind.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:25.650
I found an IRL idiot.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:29.300
This is why you'll always 
be tasked with grunt work.

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:30.550
I-Itsuki...

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.070
What's wrong?

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:34.840
Hey, Musashi.

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.300
What, pest?

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:38.560
Are you Yu-chan?

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:41.060
Yu-chan?

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.340
Wha... you... Yu-chan is...

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:44.690
Oh, sorry.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.690
You're Sasaki Yutaka-kun.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.310
What?

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.600
You completely exposed his identity.

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:59.780
Words are the mirror reflecting reality.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.450
Sometimes they become a blade. How sad.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.630
Now he's done it.

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:04.900
Did he troll the troll?

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:07.010
I feel kind of sorry for him now.

00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:08.780
Who does that, though?

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:09.380
What?

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:13.210
So this is the reason 
Sasaki-kun's not here today.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:17.850
I stopped by his room this morning, 
but he didn't even answer.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.220
This isn't good.

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:22.220
If he stops coming to school,

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:25.640
it will hurt <i>PSO2</i>'s image with the school.

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:29.090
You need to reconcile with him
 so he'll come to school.

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:30.320
That's an order.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:32.650
What? What am I supposed to do?

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:36.650
You sowed the seeds. You deal with it.

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:38.410
But...

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.530
Yu-chan, open the door.

00:17:41.050 --> 00:17:43.060
Shut up! Leave me alone!

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:44.400
Yu-chan.

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:46.040
What should I do?

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:47.380
Oh, right.

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:49.920
We're not just connected in real life.

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:00.470
Yu-chan.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:07.850
Itsuki

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:07.850
I think of you as my friend.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:11.360
Come on out.

00:18:12.160 --> 00:18:13.270
Shut up.

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:17.240
<i>PSO2</i> was the only place 
where I could be myself.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:18.990
Yu-chan.

00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:21.300
You wouldn't understand.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.670
In real life, nothing I do ever goes right,

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:25.660
and no one ever acknowledges me.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.100
But you...

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:30.300
I... I envied you!

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:35.760
At least let me do what I want in <i>PSO2</i>!

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:37.510
You can't!

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:42.040
There are people in real life and 
in <i>PSO2</i>, and they're connected.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:44.260
You can't live life doing as you please.

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:49.020
Besides, if you run now, you won't 
belong anywhere in here or in reality.

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:51.020
So...

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:54.020
...come back.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:18:58.900
Yu-chan!

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:02.160
I told you to stop calling me Yu-chan.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:05.660
I've always been afraid of being disliked.

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:09.840
I always tried to be patient 
and never spoke back to anyone.

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:15.000
That's why I wanted to be
 my true self in <i>PSO2</i>.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.360
But you're just acting tough.

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:18.670
It's not the real you.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:19.860
What?

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:23.000
The real Yu-chan is a nice guy.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:24.320
Tachibana-kun.

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:29.680
But I've been so mean to everyone.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:33.060
It'll all work out. No big deal.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:35.380
What?

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:37.510
I'm sorry

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:39.820
for everything!

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:42.950
Musashi feels bad about what he did, too.

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:45.450
Please forgive him.

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:48.400
Out of respect for Itsuki-kun, I forgive you.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:49.820
I forgive you.

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:51.960
Hate the sin, not the sinner.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:56.460
Don't do anything bad anymore.

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:58.670
Thank you!

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:02.670
See? If you do something bad, 
you just need to offer a sincere apology.

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:03.510
Yeah.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:06.190
Now that that's settled,

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:09.720
let us join our souls as one 
and embark on a new adventure!

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:09.720
Hey, that's my character...

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:13.130
All right! I'll lead the van—

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:16.920
I'll defeat all our enemies!

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:19.460
You guys can sit there
 and twiddle your thumbs!

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:27.140
He doesn't seem to have 
changed much, but oh well.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:27.990
Ouch.

00:20:28.280 --> 00:20:31.790
I applaud you for reaping 
the seeds you sowed.

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:33.080
What?

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:45.590
President, why did you ask me to come here?

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:49.040
I read your report.

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:51.100
Sasaki-kun has returned to school, too.

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:52.360
Yeah.

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:55.500
I think Yu-chan and I 
will become good friends.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:56.100
Why?

00:20:56.850 --> 00:21:00.860
I realized that by getting to know him
 in real life and the game,

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:05.110
we can become better friends.

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:06.860
Um...

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:08.210
Yes?

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:10.760
There's something I wanted to tell you.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.050
You know SORO, don't you?

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.680
Of course.

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:17.540
The truth is, I... I am...

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:19.540
I'm SORO!

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:21.300
I'm SORO!

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:23.120
I'm SORO!

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:28.550
A-Are you surprised?

00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:32.060
No, I knew.

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:33.800
What? How?

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:35.460
"The seeds you sowed."

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:36.060
What?

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:38.950
And then there's "connecting with 
others through association."

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:43.320
You tend to use the same phrases,
 so it just clicked.

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:44.840
I-I...

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:47.820
"Now let's embark on an endless adventure!"

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:52.650
"Don't be afraid to fail. 
Be proud of who you are."

00:21:52.650 --> 00:21:53.950
There was that, too.

00:21:54.740 --> 00:21:56.690
What else was there?

00:21:56.690 --> 00:21:58.080
H-Hey! Stop that!

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:01.040
"Run like the wind and 
dance like the flames."

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:03.650
"Whether friend or foe, sense 
your surroundings at all times."

00:22:03.650 --> 00:22:07.080
You're not supposed to bring what 
happens in the game into real life!

00:22:07.080 --> 00:22:09.840
Tachibana-kun, wait!

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:40.690
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:40.690 --> 00:24:09.300
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:42.450 --> 00:23:44.790
I'm glad everyone forgave me.

00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:46.430
I told you it would work out.

00:23:46.430 --> 00:23:50.790
Yeah, and I'm glad my vocabulary was 
within acceptable broadcast language.

00:23:50.790 --> 00:23:52.670
Acceptable broadcast language?

00:23:52.670 --> 00:23:54.130
Have you said even worse things?

00:23:54.130 --> 00:23:55.490
Well,

00:23:55.490 --> 00:24:00.070
normally I say **** or ****.

00:24:00.070 --> 00:24:01.810
We censored those, right?

00:24:01.810 --> 00:24:03.150
And that's not all.

00:24:03.150 --> 00:24:07.670
I've even used **** and **** 
in an argument before.

00:24:07.670 --> 00:24:09.300
Yu-chan, stop!
